# Declared inputs and library cells

The input fingerprint participates in cache keys. The library cell contributes
source code to its consumers but never executes as a separate process.

```python {#statistics role=lib}
import csv
from pathlib import Path

def read_measurements(path):
    with Path(path).open(encoding="utf-8", newline="") as stream:
        return [
            {"sensor": row["sensor"], "value": float(row["value"])}
            for row in csv.DictReader(stream)
        ]

def mean(values):
    return sum(values) / len(values)
```

```python {#load independent=true tags=data uses=statistics}
rows = read_measurements("data/measurements.csv")
ctx.rows = rows
ctx.average = mean([row["value"] for row in rows])
ctx.output_name = "measurements" + ".csv"
print(f"Loaded {len(rows)} declared measurements")
```

```python {#report depends-on=load tags=report}
display.csv(ctx.rows, name=ctx.output_name)
display.markdown(f"Average measurement: **{ctx.average:.2f}**", "average.md")
```

```python {#verify-composition role=test test-of=report uses=statistics}
assert len(ctx.rows) == 4
assert mean([row["value"] for row in ctx.rows]) == ctx.average
assert outputs.path("report", ctx.output_name).is_file()
```
